The spec says:
- The function `find_entity(author: dict)` must attempt author resolution in the following priority order: name with birth and death dates, alternate_names with birth and death dates, surname with birth and death dates.
- When both `birth_date` and `death_date` are present, they must be used to disambiguate records
- When either is absent, fall back to case-insensitive name matching alone
- Matching must be case-insensitive
- Support wildcards (`*` as multi-character wildcard)
- A match via `alternate_names` requires both `birth_date` and `death_date` to be present
- A match via `surname` requires both `birth_date` and `death_date` to be present
- If no valid match found, return a new author candidate dictionary
- Year comparison only considers year component
- `find_author` returns list of candidates; `find_entity` delegates to `find_author` and returns existing or None
- `MockSite.regex_ilike` needs to be added for ILIKE semantics

